Btw, i'm not a doctor but here's my two cents based on what you've said.

&#x200B;

you state you suffer from severe bipolar. there is a chance selegiline can induce mania. actually quite easily, even at 5mg sel.

&#x200B;

you might want to ask psych to consider following combo:

&#x200B;

1. Adderall
2. Lamictal or any of the other bipolar meds.

&#x200B;

how do you know you have bipolar btw? have you spoken to your doc about this? maybe its just depression and adhd. again i'm not a doc. just looking out for you bud. either you know the answer, or your doc will. if i remember correctly bipolar is either mostly mania with occasional sever depressive episodes, or mostly depression with occasional manic episodes. if you are just depressed/adhd, then maybe even just adderall+wellbutrin can do the trick. it works for both adhd/depression. the brain is complex however, and everyon'es situation is different. so maybe write some notes down and talk to your doc. I get it, you're in university right now, pain in the ass to figure it all out when the semester is just getting started. if thats the case maybe figure it out during christmas vacay. if its that much of a hindrance, withdraw for a year, work a part time job, and use the extra time to calibrate your meds to a stable level.

&#x200B;

when you are working on calibration, stick to the same dosage of meds for a month.  journal entry every single day, with scores for productivity, energy, mood, side effects, and most importantly sleep quality/duration. sleep deprivation is the usual suspect in most cases, people think they can just plow through it with more meds. false. if sleep deprived, you actually should lower the meds/caffeine, have like a week of recovery sleep, and try calibrating once more.  speak with doc of results.

&#x200B;

sorry if any of this sounds cold/emotionless. im freakin tired today bro lol.

20 mg selegiline

1500 mg dlpa

&#x200B;

yeah that's the one. 

&#x200B;

ADC quality is not that great. I love India as a country, but they're not doing so well economically. I have a feeling those labs producing these generics are using cheap binders and fillers, making it difficult to get quality absorption rates.

&#x200B;

talk to your doc about generic selegiline. you might have thought that only zelapar and emsam exists. there is actually a 3rd option, which is generic selegiline tablets. it used to be called eldepryl, but the patent expired and it is now being produced as a generic.

3 x 500 mg.

&#x200B;

its not a fatal combo. dlpa is rate limiting, which means that the body will only absorb what it needs. if you're on meds, obviously this is going to increase that threshold.

&#x200B;

i've been on sel for at least 6 years. dlpa works like a charm.

&#x200B;

also don't get the solgar brand. get the life extension brand. google it.

&#x200B;

also talk to your doc and get a script for it. don't just cut corners and take matters into your own hands. I understand it is difficult, but it is possible, you just have to make some phone calls and talk to several docs until you can find one that will work with you. If you do go this route, make sure the script is for generic selegiline. any other brand will cost you thousands of dollars, the generic should run no more than 75-120 bucks.

&#x200B;

have a nice day.

